<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Nikki</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1898 CE (approx.) · capital Nikki</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading Bariba kingdom of Borgu, famed for its cavalry aristocracy and the Gaani festival still celebrated in northern Benin.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nikki was founded by Wasangari horsemen who imposed their rule on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bariba">Bariba</a> farming communities of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a>, probably in the 16th century. Its kings traced descent from Sunon Sero and through him to the legendary conqueror <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kisra-borgu-tradition">Kisra</a>. Nikki came to be recognised as the most powerful of the Borgu states, alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bussa">Kingdom of Bussa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Sina Boko, the king of Nikki, ruled with princes and Wasangari warriors who held provinces and lived from tribute and raiding. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a> cavalry checked the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a>; Sero Kpera of Nikki died fighting the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ilorin-emirate">Ilorin</a> forces in the 1830s. The annual Gaani festival renewed loyalty to the king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> raced to sign treaties at Nikki in 1894, and the Anglo-French Convention of 1898 assigned it to France. It became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-dahomey">French Dahomey</a>, and the king of Nikki remains a respected traditional ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1898 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.92%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1898 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nikki</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sero Kpera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Bariba traditional religion and Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Baatonum</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/benin">Benin</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nikki, Borgu (Nikki)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1699&amp;focus=kingdom-of-nikki" aria-label="Kingdom of Nikki on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4768 1807 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Nikki lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5088 2063L5072 2192"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5072 2192h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5088 2063h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5088 2063h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nikki. <a href="/atlas?year=1699&amp;focus=kingdom-of-nikki">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
